  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying two purely imaginary numbers is similar to multiplying two monomials. We also use the fact that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-6\\text{i})\\cdot 2\\text{i} & =(-6)\\cdot 2\\cdot {\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =-12\\,{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =(-12)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
